Package: qiblalab
Title: Reproducible Analysis of Early Islamic Mosque Orientations
Version: 0.0.0.9000
Authors@R: c(
    person("Christiaan", "Pauw",
           email = "christiaan.pauw@nova.org.za",
           role  = c("aut", "cre")),
    person("Dan", "Gibson",
           role    = "dtc",
           comment = "Source dataset: Early Islamic Qibla Database 2021, https://doi.org/10.6084/m9.figshare.13570655.v2"))
Description: Tools for reproducible testing of competing hypotheses about the
    development of the Islamic qibla (prayer direction). Imports and documents Dan
    Gibson's Early Islamic Qibla Database, computes geodesic bearings, applies
    circular statistics, and provides a structured hypothesis-testing framework.
    All analytical decisions are explicit and auditable. The package is a neutral
    analytical instrument: it does not assume any candidate destination is correct.
